  "term": "Celexa",
  "definition": "Celexa is citalopram hydrobromide, an antidepressant medicine taken by mouth. It is a selective serotonin reuptake inhibitor that increases serotonin activity in the central nervous system, with little effect on norepinephrine or dopamine reuptake.",
